This folder is a test & demonstration platform for both standalone
GDB command-line debugging and for Visual Studio Code debugging.  As such,
it demonstrates the production environment, rather than the development
environment.

So, in order for make to work properly, you first need to go to the cbl-gdb
folder and run "make && sudo make install", because this Makefile goes for
/usr/local/bin/ rather than the cbl-gdb/ development executables.

Bob Dubner, 2020-01-31
